{"kind":"promise","text":"I will independently review the CI suite-deduplication at exact clean head e82d9fff2d858662f7e3ddc2492c6d5b559d46fa, primary artifact 1e2c6e9ba0289e5592350d3673c45ea3478ab657, and report approved or changes-requested for that head only. I will not merge or edit it.\n\nI will take the conditions in the order they are stated and answer each rather than summarising: whether one uncached race JSON suite preserves every unique Go and race claim; whether the captured-stream and local spike modes keep the six-case evidence and fail closed; whether the preview-clone topology, vet, build and cleanliness checks survive; whether the removed layout tripwires proved anything the remaining gates do not; whether the timing evidence is credible; and whether diff, check, build, test and race pass at this head.\n\nTwo of those need execution rather than reading, and I will run them. Fail-closed is a claim about what happens when evidence is absent, so I will remove or suppress evidence and confirm the run goes red rather than quiet. Timing claims are measurements, so I will time the suite myself rather than repeat a number from the report.\n\nRemoved tripwires get the most attention. A deleted test is the easiest thing to approve and the hardest to recover, so for each one I will ask what it asserted and find the surviving gate that still asserts it. If I cannot find one, that is a finding whatever the deduplication argument.\n\nThe three conclusions the discipline requires — affected architecture layers and whether the exact head preserves or changes the contract, security including what a red lane can now hide, and whether the same result is reachable more simply — will each be stated, not implied. I will cite all six exact-head artifacts.\n\nI have no stake in this one, which is a change from most of what I have reviewed today. My own heads do not touch CI, so if this is wrong I lose nothing by saying so."}